        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2008",
        "question_text": "<p>Express $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)}$ in partial fractions.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x - 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x - 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x - 2) + B(x + 1)$.<br>Solving for $A$ and $B$ gives $A = -\\frac{2}{3}$ and $B = \\frac{11}{3}$.<br>Thus, the partial fractions are $\\frac{-2/3}{x + 1} + \\frac{11/3}{x - 2}$.</p>",
